@startuml
title ThingsBoard 3.6 OTA 包保存、分配、状态通知与 MQTT 分块下载

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontColor #111827
skinparam ArrowColor #253746
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #334155
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
skinparam ActorBorderColor #334155
skinparam ActorBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam DatabaseBorderColor #7C2D12
skinparam DatabaseBackgroundColor #FFF7D6
skinparam QueueBorderColor #176B87
skinparam QueueBackgroundColor #E8F3F8
skinparam NoteBorderColor #7C2D12
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFF7D6
skinparam SequenceGroupBorderColor #374151
skinparam SequenceGroupBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
skinparam BoxBorderColor #475569
skinparam BoxBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam maxMessageSize 130

actor "Tenant Admin" as Admin
participant "REST Controllers\nPackage / Device / Profile" as REST
participant "Application + DAO\nServices" as Service
database "PostgreSQL\nota_package / device\ndevice_profile" as PG
participant "OTA State\nService" as State
queue "OTA Queue\ntb_ota_package" as Queue
participant "Core OTA\nConsumer" as Consumer
participant "Telemetry +\nAttribute Service" as Telemetry
participant "Device Actor\nattribute subscription" as Actor
actor "MQTT Device" as Device
participant "MQTT Transport" as MQTT
participant "Transport API +\nData Cache" as API

== Phase A: package metadata and binary ==
Admin -> REST: POST /api/otaPackage\nmetadata + usesUrl
activate REST
REST -> Service: save(request, user)
activate Service
Service -> PG: INSERT/UPDATE ota_package metadata
activate PG
PG --> Service: COMMIT metadata row\nmay have data IS NULL
deactivate PG
Service -> Service: evict metadata/data cache\npublish SaveEntityEvent + action
Service --> REST: OtaPackageInfo(hasData)
deactivate Service
REST --> Admin: HTTP 200
deactivate REST

opt binary package uploaded in second request
  Admin -> REST: multipart POST /api/otaPackage/{id}
  REST -> REST: MultipartFile.getBytes()
  REST -> Service: saveOtaPackageData(full byte[])
  Service -> Service: generate + validate checksum\nvalidate tenant quota
  Service -> PG: UPDATE same row\ndata OID + file metadata
  PG --> Service: COMMIT
  Service -> Service: evict otaPackagesData
  Service --> REST: OtaPackageInfo(hasData=true)
  REST --> Admin: HTTP 200
end

note over REST,PG
Metadata and binary are separate transactions.
The upload, hash and JPA entity all materialize the full byte array.
end note

== Phase B: Device or Profile assignment ==
Admin -> REST: POST Device or DeviceProfile\nfirmwareId/softwareId
activate REST
REST -> Service: save entity
Service -> PG: validate full package + save pointer
PG --> Service: pointer COMMIT
Service -> State: update(saved, old)
activate State
State -> State: effective id = Device override\nelse Profile fallback

par fire-and-forget Queue branch
  State ->> Queue: ToOtaPackageStateServiceMsg\nrandom UUID key, callback=null
else asynchronous Telemetry branch
  State ->> Telemetry: target_* + state=QUEUED
end
State --> Service: return without joining branches
deactivate State
Service --> REST: saved entity
REST --> Admin: HTTP response
deactivate REST

Queue -> Consumer: poll pack
activate Consumer
Consumer -> State: process(message)
activate State
State -> PG: reload Device + Profile
PG --> State: current effective package
alt queued target is stale or Device removed
  State --> Consumer: false
  Consumer -> Consumer: skip; pack will still commit
else target is still current
  State ->> Telemetry: state=INITIATED
  State --> Consumer: true immediately after scheduling Future
end
deactivate State
Consumer -> Queue: commit whole polled pack
deactivate Consumer

opt target was accepted
  ... INITIATED callback may run before or after Queue commit ...
  Telemetry -->> State: success or failure callback
  State ->> Telemetry: save/remove fw_* or sw_*\nShared Attributes
  Telemetry ->> Actor: DeviceAttributesEventNotificationMsg\nafter attribute save succeeds
  Actor ->> Device: attribute notification\nonly if session subscribed
end

note over Queue,Consumer
Only synchronous process() exceptions are caught and logged.
Async Telemetry/Attribute failures happen outside this catch and do not retry the Queue record.
end note

== Phase C: MQTT binary chunk ==
Device -> MQTT: PUBLISH v2/fw/request/42/chunk/0\npayload 16384
activate MQTT
alt requestId already bound in this connection
  MQTT -> API: get(packageId, 16384, 0)
else first chunk for requestId
  MQTT -> API: GetOtaPackageRequestMsg(Device,type)\nvia Transport API request/reply Queue
  activate API
  API -> PG: load Device, Profile, OtaPackageInfo
  PG --> API: effective binary package metadata
  alt URL package or missing target
    API --> MQTT: FAILURE / NOT_FOUND
    MQTT -> Device: error topic + close session
  else binary package
    API -> API: cache.has(packageId)
    opt cache miss
      API -> PG: load full OID binary
      PG --> API: byte[]
      API -> API: cache.put(full byte[])
    end
    API --> MQTT: SUCCESS + package id + metadata
    MQTT -> MQTT: otaPackSessions[42] = packageId
  end
  deactivate API
end

MQTT --> Device: PUBACK before cache range read
MQTT -> API: cache.get(packageId, 16384, 0)
API --> MQTT: chunk bytes
MQTT ->> Device: PUBLISH v2/fw/response/42/chunk/0
deactivate MQTT

loop remaining chunks use same requestId
  Device -> MQTT: request chunk N
  MQTT -> API: range read cached package id
  API --> MQTT: bytes
  MQTT ->> Device: response chunk N
end

Device ->> Telemetry: fw_state DOWNLOADING / VERIFIED / UPDATED / FAILED
note over Device,Telemetry
Generic device telemetry has no server-side transition validator.
LwM2M uses a separate Object 5/9 state machine.
end note

note over PG,Device
Pointer DB, Queue, target/state telemetry, Shared Attributes,
Actor delivery, binary chunks and final device result do not share a transaction.
end note

@enduml
